          <solution>
              <p>Take the phrase: twinkle twinkle little star.
                            Store each word in a separate variable, then print out the sentence on
                            one line using print.</p>
    <program interactive="activecode" language="python" label="var-wc-rhymeq-sol"><code>
# Set each word to its own variable
word1 = "twinkle"
word2 = "little"
word3 = "star"

# Print each word in succession
# Using commas automaticallly inserts spaces
print(word1, word1, word2, word3)

#another option is
#print(word1 + " " + word1 + " " + word2 + " " + word3)
        </code>
        </program>
